849cc23b6","clm_83ac5da94762939e603a1f3c8de18751326c883212be1f91ba75b9281a196049","clm_a1a4692a07a47c5a390306622ba5d6831a7c2387dc56bb1ad9af16920a256934","clm_a4795b7829a32e794d7ffaa6710fc796bae5316f23f6a7b22d0b3d60fba598e9","clm_de70252ddfbb707f3760df8955f60a739f681e71e19939772634fdbc98dafdb1"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:18:50Z","created_by_operation":"op_2be23d4685b745c394c83e37e7cf3309","id":"pg_295b021f9c31530ba6138e3591ab19fe","maturity":"draft","page_type":"entity","path":"pages/entities/the-open-engine-zeroshot-8e3591ab19fe.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":[],"title":"the-open-engine/zeroshot","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:18:50Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2be23d4685b745c394c83e37e7cf3309"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0b36816531b234873ae6b87619536c3d41015b7014f52bae6ea833c7181fe4a4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Three execution targets share the same graph and runtime plan: local mode in the current Git worktree reusing Codex or Claude Code logins, a self-hosted Docker target image bundling the engine plus pinned Codex and Claude harness CLIs, and a managed Zeroshot Cloud target."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0c374aeaa18fbc6ff6b01e3a2e06bef25ff39748067004a4a869353ca43ae0ea"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product is a native `zeroshot` executable (v8 hard cutover, former Node.js runtime retired), installed via npm and providing commands like `zeroshot run`, `zeroshot version`, and `zeroshot template list/show`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3d7f16957cc3edf5b02e5eb85c29ab46993c957f3da6345feb27984c9b136078"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors run `npm ci`, `npm run check`, and `cargo test --workspace`; Node.js is repository tooling and the npm delivery mechanism only."},{"claim_ids":["clm_40fc69a90fc002613f7a30a1c6064415511c6b0478f2b0a5eab373826fffe3c5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A Python SDK is provided with public objects including LocalTarget, DirectTarget, HostedTarget, Target, Preset, GraphSpec, UniformRuntime, RuntimePlan, RunRequest, and MergePlanRequest."},{"claim_ids":["clm_44cf8958e4c800f453c1a19c8554b615d2ed9a324fbda16a9e7d5ebf8ec742ec"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The built-in software-change graph gives the goal to a worker, runs acceptance and code review in parallel, routes rejections to a repair worker with repeated reviews, and delivers accepted changes through Git, CI, and merge, routing delivery conflicts back through repair."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5e8d6d2cd50de0453cfb951f727b93071589e7c5f0dbcc7b3e2ab91ab8bd7145"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The npm package installs a verified native binary for Linux x64/arm64, macOS x64/arm64, and Windows x64; native archives and SHA256 checksums are attached to each canonical vX.Y.Z GitHub Release."},{"claim_ids":["clm_818463f4c2fa684eb98b22c72ada80d4bbad26936c4723c22692fa2849cc23b6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Every graph transition event is written to a durable SQLite ledger; after validating graph, runtime plan, and input, Zeroshot opens a durable ledger recording each node result."},{"claim_ids":["clm_83ac5da94762939e603a1f3c8de18751326c883212be1f91ba75b9281a196049"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Control flow is authored data rather than hidden in prompts: sequence, parallel review, retry paths, delivery, and exit conditions are explicit before a run starts, and no runtime agent chooses the next step."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a4795b7829a32e794d7ffaa6710fc796bae5316f23f6a7b22d0b3d60fba598e9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Zeroshot turns a software goal into an explicit multi-agent graph: one agent implements, independent agents review, failures route into bounded repair, and delivery happens only after the graph's checks pass."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0b36816531b234873ae6b87619536c3d41015b7014f52bae6ea833c7181fe4a4","clm_0c374aeaa18fbc6ff6b01e3a2e06bef25ff39748067004a4a869353ca43ae0ea","clm_3d7f16957cc3edf5b02e5eb85c29ab46993c957f3da6345feb27984c9b136078","clm_40fc69a90fc002613f7a30a1c6064415511c6b0478f2b0a5eab373826fffe3c5","clm_44cf8958e4c800f453c1a19c8554b615d2ed9a324fbda16a9e7d5ebf8ec742ec","clm_5e8d6d2cd50de0453cfb951f727b93071589e7c5f0dbcc7b3e2ab91ab8bd7145","clm_818463f4c2fa684eb98b22c72ada80d4bbad26936c4723c22692fa2849cc23b6","clm_83ac5da94762939e603a1f3c8de18751326c883212be1f91ba75b9281a196049","clm_a4795b7829a32e794d7ffaa6710fc796bae5316f23f6a7b22d0b3d60fba598e9"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:18:50Z","created_by_operation":"op_2be23d4685b745c394c83e37e7cf3309","id":"pg_688508621263506586b3491a1416edcd","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/the-open-engine-zeroshot-readme-md-b550c15279c9-491a1416edcd.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_52f9aac99ed75406b7827ef4d501d57b"],"title":"the-open-engine/zeroshot/README.md @ b550c15279c9","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:18:50Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2be23d4685b745c394c83e37e7cf3309"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_05b338388db00e1953361e1fec360ebd07ee8cdf92a5aee08d3f298e53a22a04"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The apply method supports dryRun, ifGeneration optimistic concurrency, and idempotencyKey parameters, suggesting the cluster API is designed for safe, repeatable graph applications."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a1a4692a07a47c5a390306622ba5d6831a7c2387dc56bb1ad9af16920a256934"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Subscription methods use generic framing: watch, logs, and agent/attach (and run/* equivalents) establish subscriptions via one JSON-RPC result, then use generic event, subscription/cancel, subscription/closed, and $/cancelRequest notifications; no method-specific event/cancel/closed methods exist on the wire."}],"claim_ids":["clm_05b338388db00e1953361e1fec360ebd07ee8cdf92a5aee08d3f298e53a22a04","clm_a1a4692a07a47c5a390306622ba5d6831a7c2387dc56bb1ad9af16920a256934"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:18:50Z","created_by_operation":"op_2be23d4685b745c394c83e37e7cf3309","id":"pg_98e04594d54658f0a509cf28b728e63c","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/the-open-engine-zeroshot-docs-reference-cluster-api-md-b550c15279c9-cf28b728e63c.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_90b0c78528935a3e8e11aa0e72f252c5"],"title":"the-open-engine/zeroshot/docs/reference/cluster/api.md @ b550c15279c9","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:18:50Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2be23d4685b745c394c83e37e7cf3309"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_40fc69a90fc002613f7a30a1c6064415511c6b0478f2b0a5eab373826fffe3c5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A Python SDK is provided with public objects including LocalTarget, DirectTarget, HostedTarget, Target, Preset, GraphSpec, UniformRuntime, RuntimePlan, RunRequest, and MergePlanRequest."}],"claim_ids":["clm_40fc69a90fc002613f7a30a1c6064415511c6b0478f2b0a5eab373826fffe3c5"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:18:50Z","created_by_operation":"op_2be23d4685b745c394c83e37e7cf3309","id":"pg_a9a95810413553e79c91d9a8a0a8dd77","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/the-open-engine-zeroshot-docs-reference-python-configuration-md-b550c1-d9a8a0a8dd77.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_db796d69c1fc52398e74d1a6b44b913e"],"title":"the-open-engine/zeroshot/docs/reference/python/configuration.md @ b550c15279c9","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:18:50Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2be23d4685b745c394c83e37e7cf3309"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0b36816531b234873ae6b87619536c3d41015b7014f52bae6ea833c7181fe4a4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Three execution targets share the same graph and runtime plan: local mode in the current Git worktree reusing Codex or Claude Code logins, a self-hosted Docker target image bundling the engine plus pinned Codex and Claude harness CLIs, and a managed Zeroshot Cloud target."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0bf189be40418d5352fa500818c5d34366893c975a0305374c19194d3d815d4e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A run consists of three authored values: a graph defining control flow and typed state, a runtime plan binding each executable node to a harness, provider, model, and named connections, and caller-owned initial input validated against the graph before execution."},{"claim_ids":["clm_246f7f6c5217275aa6f4507f546b7ae82c5504c858d4240f3bc115fd1fce90a0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Besides the software-change template, a single-worker template exists for work that does not need the review loop, and custom graphs follow the same protocol contracts."},{"claim_ids":["clm_818463f4c2fa684eb98b22c72ada80d4bbad26936c4723c22692fa2849cc23b6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Every graph transition event is written to a durable SQLite ledger; after validating graph, runtime plan, and input, Zeroshot opens a durable ledger recording each node result."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0b36816531b234873ae6b87619536c3d41015b7014f52bae6ea833c7181fe4a4","clm_0bf189be40418d5352fa500818c5d34366893c975a0305374c19194d3d815d4e","clm_246f7f6c5217275aa6f4507f546b7ae82c5504c858d4240f3bc115fd1fce90a0","clm_818463f4c2fa684eb98b22c72ada80d4bbad26936c4723c22692fa2849cc23b6"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:18:50Z","created_by_operation":"op_2be23d4685b745c394c83e37e7cf3309","id":"pg_c6cea27f1c535db8b10c2072b80aca3c","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/the-open-engine-zeroshot-docs-index-md-b550c15279c9-2072b80aca3c.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_9e6d59903dd75171b4088f2fa3c55749"],"title":"the-open-engine/zeroshot/docs/index.md @ b550c15279c9","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:18:50Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2be23d4685b745c394c83e37e7cf3309"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1e78f5ad236b981937399a0a2c600ce61826b2de844ff2aa0c9369a95b00ea6e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: releases publish one canonical version across GitHub tag, native archives, checksum manifest, npm package, target image, Python wheels, and versioned docs via a release workflow using GitHub OIDC trusted publishing, with no long-lived npm or PyPI tokens."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5e8d6d2cd50de0453cfb951f727b93071589e7c5f0dbcc7b3e2ab91ab8bd7145"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The npm package installs a verified native binary for Linux x64/arm64, macOS x64/arm64, and Windows x64; native archives and SHA256 checksums are attached to each canonical vX.Y.Z GitHub Release."},{"claim_ids":["clm_de70252ddfbb707f3760df8955f60a739f681e71e19939772634fdbc98dafdb1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: release jobs verify already-published immutable artifacts before completing missing steps, and recovery must use the same version, tag, and source commit without overwriting different artifacts."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1e78f5ad236b981937399a0a2c600ce61826b2de844ff2aa0c9369a95b00ea6e","clm_5e8d6d2cd50de0453cfb951f727b93071589e7c5f0dbcc7b3e2ab91ab8bd7145","clm_de70252ddfbb707f3760df8955f60a739f681e71e19939772634fdbc98dafdb1"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:18:50Z","created_by_operation":"op_2be23d4685b745c394c83e37e7cf3309","id":"pg_e84cbaa0ca9252a98d18c11451143708","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/the-open-engine-zeroshot-publishing-md-b550c15279c9-c11451143708.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_7f9af73b820450c1915da1e829aee56b"],"title":"the-open-engine/zeroshot/PUBLISHING.md @ b550c15279c9","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:18:50Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2be23d4685b745c394c83e37e7cf3309"}
